IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Wiring Work) Regulations 2024 (S 559/2024), made by the Info-communications Media Development Authority with the Minister's approval under section 97 of the Act
-- (the 2020 Revised Edition's number for the regulation-making power the 2000 Edition numbers section 74), made 26 June 2024, FIRST PUBLISHED 28 June 2024 at 5 pm, in operation 1 July 2024 (reg 1);
-- and its amendment, the Telecommunications (Wiring Work) (Amendment) Regulations 2024 (S 852/2024), made 7 November 2024, first published 8 November 2024 at 5 pm, in operation 11 November 2024.
-- Deposited 2026-11-04 from the e-Gazette's follow-up list into subjects/sg/telecommunications-wiring-work-regulations-2024/registers/source-bundle/ (TA1999-WW-S559-2024, TA1999-WW-S852-2024).
--
-- DO THEY REPLACE THE INTERNAL WIRING REGULATIONS 2005 (S 479/2005)?  Yes, from 1 July 2024: reg 10(1) reads "Revoke the Telecommunications (Internal Wiring) Regulations 2005 (G.N. No. S 479/2005)", and the new Regulations are in operation
-- on 1 July 2024.  Reg 10 has only two sub-regulations, the revocation and a saving for individuals with optical fibre cable experience (reg 10(2)); the deposited text contains no provision that continues a licence granted under the 2005 Regulations,
-- and none is encoded here.  The 2005 Regulations are encoded in sgta-i-iw-wiring.l4, whose reg 1 function runs from 21 July 2005 with no end; the function below, `IW Regulations 2005: in operation on the date, until revoked on 1 July 2024`, gives the end.
-- The Composition of Offences Regulations (S 560/2024, sgta-i-comp.l4) cross-refers to both: para (f) now reads "Internal Wiring Regulations 2005 as in force before 1 July 2024" and a new para (h) names reg 6 of these Regulations.
--
-- WHAT THEY DO.  They license, by class licence under section 5 of the Act, the individuals ("licensed installers") and businesses ("licensed contractors") who carry out "wiring work": installing, modifying, maintaining or repairing wiring that is or is
-- intended to be used for connection to a licensee's telecommunication system and that is not done by or for the licensee.  They do not mention receivers, broadcasting or radio-communication equipment, and they do not touch ss 53 to 56 of the Act.
-- No answer to the receiver question depends on them.  Before 1 July 2024 these Regulations answer NOTHING.  The reading day is not modelled (published three days before they are in operation; S 852/2024 published 8 November and in operation 11 November 2024).

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:28 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 97 of the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:29 | Telecommunications Act 1999, the Info‑communications Media
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:30 | Development Authority, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:31 | Communications and Information, makes the following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:33 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:34 | 1. These Regulations are the Telecommunications (Wiring Work)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:35 | Regulations 2024 and come into operation on 1 July 2024.
@ref WW regs: enacting words and regulation 1 (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:28-35)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 1 July 2024)` MEANS d AT LEAST (Date 1 7 2024)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW Regulations 2005: in operation on the date, until revoked on 1 July 2024` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 21 7 2005) AND d LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024)

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:37 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:38 | 2. In these Regulations —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:39 | “Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work” means
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:40 | the code of practice issued by the Authority under section 30
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:41 | of the Act setting out the technical standards and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:44 | specifications for the performance or carrying out of wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:45 | work;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:46 | “licence” means a telecommunication wiring installer class
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:47 | licence or a telecommunication wiring contractor class
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:48 | licence;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:49 | “licensed contractor” means a person who holds a
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:50 | telecommunication wiring contractor class licence;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:51 | “licensed installer” means an individual who holds a
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:52 | telecommunication wiring installer class licence;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:53 | “telecommunication wiring contractor class licence” means a
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:54 | class licence mentioned in regulation 5 and granted by the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:55 | Authority under section 5 of the Act;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:56 | “telecommunication wiring installer class licence” means a class
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:57 | licence mentioned in regulation 4 and granted by the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:58 | Authority under section 5 of the Act;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:59 | “user” means a person who has subscribed to or intends to
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:60 | subscribe to any telecommunication service provided by a
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:61 | telecommunication system licensee;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:62 | “wiring work” means the installation, modification,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:63 | maintenance or repair of any wiring —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:64 | (a) that is or is intended to be used for connection to any
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:65 | telecommunication system of a telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:66 | system licensee; and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:67 | (b) that is not carried out by or on behalf of the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:68 | telecommunication system licensee.
@ref WW reg 2: definitions (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:37-68)
GIVEN `the person holds a telecommunication wiring contractor class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 2: the person is a "licensed contractor"` MEANS `the person holds a telecommunication wiring contractor class licence`

GIVEN `the individual holds a telecommunication wiring installer class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 2: the individual is a "licensed installer"` MEANS `the individual holds a telecommunication wiring installer class licence`

GIVEN `the wiring is or is intended to be used for connection to a telecommunication system of a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is carried out by or on behalf of the telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is installation, modification, maintenance or repair` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 2: the work is "wiring work"` MEANS
        `the work is installation, modification, maintenance or repair`
    AND `the wiring is or is intended to be used for connection to a telecommunication system of a telecommunication system licensee`
    AND NOT `the work is carried out by or on behalf of the telecommunication system licensee`

GIVEN `the person has subscribed to or intends to subscribe to a telecommunication service provided by a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 2: the person is a "user"` MEANS `the person has subscribed to or intends to subscribe to a telecommunication service provided by a telecommunication system licensee`

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:70 | Application to be licensed installer and licensed contractor
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:71 | 3.—(1) An individual who satisfies any of the following
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:72 | requirements may apply to be a licensed installer by submitting to
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:73 | the Authority the items specified in paragraph (3):
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:74 | (a) the individual has, in relation to a type of wiring specified
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:75 | in the first column of the First Schedule, any of the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:76 | corresponding qualifications specified in the second
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:77 | column of that Schedule for carrying out wiring work;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:80 | (b) the individual has carried out any specified work on behalf
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:81 | of a telecommunication system licensee for the minimum
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:82 | specified period (whether or not the individual is employed
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:83 | by the telecommunication system licensee at the time of
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:84 | application).
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:85 | (2) A person —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:86 | (a) who is or has employed a licensed installer; and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:87 | (b) who, for profit or reward, intends to carry on or carries on
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:88 | the business of providing wiring work,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:89 | may apply to be a licensed contractor by submitting to the Authority
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:90 | the items specified in paragraph (3).
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:91 | (3) The items mentioned in paragraphs (1) and (2) are as follows:
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:92 | (a) in the case of an application to be a licensed installer,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:93 | information on the type of wiring in relation to which the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:94 | individual is qualified to carry out wiring work;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:95 | (b) in the case of an application to be a licensed contractor,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:96 | information on the type of wiring in relation to which the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:97 | person provides or intends to provide wiring work;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:98 | (c) payment to the Authority of the appropriate fee specified in
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:99 | the Second Schedule;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:100 | (d) any written information that the Authority may require for
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:101 | the purpose of the application.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:102 | (4) An individual mentioned in paragraph (1) who has submitted
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:103 | the items specified in paragraph (3) to the Authority may be
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:104 | registered by the Authority as a licensed installer and is deemed, on
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:105 | the date of the registration, to be granted a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:106 | installer class licence.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:107 | (5) A person mentioned in paragraph (2) who has submitted the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:108 | items specified in paragraph (3) to the Authority may be registered by
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:109 | the Authority as a licensed contractor and is deemed, on the date of
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:110 | the registration, to be granted a telecommunication wiring contractor
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:111 | class licence.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:114 | (6) In this regulation —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:115 | “minimum specified period” means a cumulative period of at
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:116 | least one year, whether the period (or any part of the period) is
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:117 | before, on or after 1 July 2024;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:118 | “specified work” means the installation, modification,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:119 | maintenance or repair of wiring that is —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:120 | (a) used or intended to be used for connection to any
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:121 | telecommunication system of a telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:122 | system licensee; and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:123 | (b) of a type specified in the first column of the First
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:124 | Schedule.
@ref WW reg 3: application to be licensed installer and licensed contractor (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:70-124)
GIVEN `the individual has, for a type of wiring in the first column of the First Schedule, a corresponding qualification in the second column` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has carried out specified work on behalf of a telecommunication system licensee for the minimum specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(1): the individual may apply to be a licensed installer` MEANS
    `the individual has, for a type of wiring in the first column of the First Schedule, a corresponding qualification in the second column`
    OR `the individual has carried out specified work on behalf of a telecommunication system licensee for the minimum specified period`

GIVEN `the person is or has employed a licensed installer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to carry on or carries on the business of providing wiring work for profit or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(2): the person may apply to be a licensed contractor` MEANS
    `the person is or has employed a licensed installer` AND `the person intends to carry on or carries on the business of providing wiring work for profit or reward`

GIVEN `the applicant has submitted the information on the type of wiring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has paid the appropriate fee specified in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has submitted any written information the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(3): the applicant has submitted the items the regulation specifies` MEANS
    `the applicant has submitted the information on the type of wiring` AND `the applicant has paid the appropriate fee specified in the Second Schedule` AND `the applicant has submitted any written information the Authority requires`

GIVEN `the cumulative period in days of specified work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(6): the period is at least the "minimum specified period" (a cumulative period of at least one year, before, on or after 1 July 2024)` MEANS
    `the cumulative period in days of specified work` AT LEAST 365  -- "at least one year" is read as 365 days; a leap year has 366, so this is the stricter reading for the applicant (assumed, not ruled)

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:126 | Telecommunication wiring installer class licence
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:127 | 4.—(1) A licensed installer is authorised to personally carry out
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:128 | wiring work, in relation to the type of wiring specified in the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:129 | application made by the licensed installer to the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:130 | regulation 3(1), with effect from the date of the grant of the licensed
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:131 | installer’s telecommunication wiring installer class licence.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:132 | (2) A licensed installer must comply with the conditions specified
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:133 | in the Third Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:135 | Telecommunication wiring contractor class licence
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:136 | 5.—(1) A licensed contractor is authorised to carry on the business
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:137 | of providing wiring work, in relation to the type of wiring specified in
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:138 | the application made by the licensed contractor to the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:139 | regulation 3(2), with effect from the date of the grant of the licensed
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:140 | contractor’s telecommunication wiring contractor class licence.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:141 | (2) A licensed contractor must comply with the conditions specified
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:142 | in the Fourth Schedule.
@ref WW regs 4 and 5: the class licences (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:126-142)
GIVEN `the individual has been registered by the Authority as a licensed installer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(4): the individual is deemed, on the date of registration, to be granted a telecommunication wiring installer class licence` MEANS
    `the individual has been registered by the Authority as a licensed installer`

GIVEN `the person has been registered by the Authority as a licensed contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 3(5): the person is deemed, on the date of registration, to be granted a telecommunication wiring contractor class licence` MEANS
    `the person has been registered by the Authority as a licensed contractor`

GIVEN `the work is in relation to the type of wiring specified in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant of the licence has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 4(1): the licensed installer is authorised to personally carry out the wiring work` MEANS
    `the work is in relation to the type of wiring specified in the application` AND `the grant of the licence has taken effect`

GIVEN `the business is in relation to the type of wiring specified in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant of the licence has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 5(1): the licensed contractor is authorised to carry on the business of providing wiring work` MEANS
    `the business is in relation to the type of wiring specified in the application` AND `the grant of the licence has taken effect`

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:144 | False or misleading information
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:145 | 6. A person who provides false, misleading or inaccurate
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:146 | information to the Authority under regulation 3(1) or (2) shall be
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:147 | guilty of an offence.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:150 | Cessation of licence
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:151 | 7. A licence ceases to be valid in respect of a licensed installer or
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:152 | licensed contractor —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:153 | (a) on the date the licensed installer or licensed contractor
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:154 | gives written notice to the Authority, in any form that the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:155 | Authority may require, that the licensed installer or
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:156 | licensed contractor has permanently ceased carrying out
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:157 | wiring work or carrying on the business of providing
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:158 | wiring work, as the case may be;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:159 | (b) in relation to a licensed contractor, on the date the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:160 | registration of the licensed contractor’s business name (if
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:161 | any), under which the licensed contractor carries on the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:162 | business of providing wiring work, under the Business
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:163 | Names Registration Act 2014 ceases or is cancelled; or
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:164 | (c) in relation to a licensed contractor that is a company
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:165 | incorporated under the Companies Act 1967 or a limited
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:166 | liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:167 | Partnerships Act 2005, on the date the licensed contractor
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:168 | goes into compulsory or voluntary liquidation other than
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:169 | for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction.
@ref WW regs 6 and 7: false or misleading information; cessation of licence (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:144-169)
GIVEN `the person provides false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority under regulation 3(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 6: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person provides false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority under regulation 3(1) or (2)`

GIVEN `the licensee has given written notice that it has permanently ceased wiring work or the business of providing wiring work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contractor's registration of its business name under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 has ceased or been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contractor is a company or limited liability partnership that has gone into compulsory or voluntary liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 7: the licence has ceased to be valid` MEANS
        `the licensee has given written notice that it has permanently ceased wiring work or the business of providing wiring work`
    OR `the contractor's registration of its business name under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 has ceased or been cancelled`
    OR `the contractor is a company or limited liability partnership that has gone into compulsory or voluntary liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:171 | Request for inspection
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:172 | 8. A user may request the Authority to inspect the wiring work
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:173 | carried out by a licensed installer or licensed contractor on the user’s
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:174 | premises to ensure that the wiring work has been carried out in
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:175 | accordance with the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:176 | Work.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:178 | Refund or remission of fees
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:179 | 9. The Authority may refund or remit the whole or part of any fee
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:180 | paid or payable under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:182 | Revocation and saving
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:183 | 10.—(1) Revoke the Telecommunications (Internal Wiring)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:184 | Regulations 2005 (G.N. No. S 479/2005).
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:187 | (2) Despite regulation 3(4) —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:188 | (a) if the Authority is satisfied that an individual has adequate
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:189 | practical experience in carrying out wiring work in relation
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:190 | to optical fibre cable (including practical experience before
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:191 | 1 July 2024), the Authority may on or after that date
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:192 | register the individual as a licensed installer to carry out
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:193 | wiring work in relation to that type of wiring; and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:194 | (b) an individual registered by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:195 | sub‑paragraph (a) is deemed to have been granted, on
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:196 | the date of the registration, a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:197 | installer class licence under regulation 3(4).
@ref WW regs 8 to 10: request for inspection; refund or remission; revocation and saving (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:171-197)
GIVEN `the individual has adequate practical experience in carrying out wiring work in relation to optical fibre cable, including before 1 July 2024, in the Authority's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW reg 10(2): the Authority may register the individual as a licensed installer for optical fibre cable, despite regulation 3(4)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 1 7 2024) AND `the individual has adequate practical experience in carrying out wiring work in relation to optical fibre cable, including before 1 July 2024, in the Authority's satisfaction`

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:199 | FIRST SCHEDULE
