-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:237 | Maintenance course conducted by
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:238 | the Singtel Training Academy.
@ref WW First Schedule: required qualifications, as made (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:199-238)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`WW First Schedule item 1 (Optical fibre cable), second column, as made by S 559/2024 (1 July 2024)` MEANS
    LIST "(a) The Certificate of Competency (CoC) in Fibre Optic Cabling conducted by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore"
       , "(b) Both of the following courses conducted by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore: (i) if completed on or before 22 December 2020, the Fibre Optics - Essential Skills for Installer course; (ii) if completed on or before 7 January 2021, the Fibre Optics - Test & Troubleshoot course"
       , "(c) The Certified Fiber Optic Technician (CFOT) course conducted by 100G Training & Consultancy Pte. Ltd."
       , "(d) The Fiber Optics Installer course conducted by FiberOpto Asia Pte. Ltd."
       , "(e) The Skill Evaluation Certificate (Knowledge) - Fibre Optics Installation conducted by James Contractor Pte. Ltd."
       , "(f) The Fibre Optic Installation and Maintenance course conducted by the Singtel Training Academy"

-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:14 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 97 of the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:15 | Telecommunications Act 1999, the Info‑communications Media
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:16 | Development Authority, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:17 | Digital Development and Information, makes the following
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:18 | Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:20 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:21 | 1. These Regulations are the Telecommunications (Wiring Work)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:22 | (Amendment) Regulations 2024 and come into operation on
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:23 | 11 November 2024.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:25 | Amendment of First Schedule
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:26 | 2. In the Telecommunications (Wiring Work) Regulations 2024
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:27 | (G.N. No. S 559/2024), in the First Schedule, in item 1, in the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:28 | second column —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:29 | (a) in paragraph (a), delete “(CoC)”;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:30 | (b) in paragraph (e), delete “or” at the end;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:31 | (c) in paragraph (f), replace the full-stop at the end with “; or”;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:32 | and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:33 | (d) after paragraph (f), insert —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:34 | “(g) The Certificate of Competency for Fibre Optics
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:35 | Cabling Installer conducted by Republic
-- src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:36 | Polytechnic.”.
@ref WW First Schedule as amended by S 852/2024 (item 1, second column) (src:TA1999-WW-S852-2024:14-36)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`WW First Schedule item 1 (Optical fibre cable), second column, as amended by S 852/2024 (11 November 2024)` MEANS
    LIST "(a) The Certificate of Competency in Fibre Optic Cabling conducted by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore"
       , "(b) Both of the following courses conducted by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore: (i) if completed on or before 22 December 2020, the Fibre Optics - Essential Skills for Installer course; (ii) if completed on or before 7 January 2021, the Fibre Optics - Test & Troubleshoot course"
       , "(c) The Certified Fiber Optic Technician (CFOT) course conducted by 100G Training & Consultancy Pte. Ltd."
       , "(d) The Fiber Optics Installer course conducted by FiberOpto Asia Pte. Ltd."
       , "(e) The Skill Evaluation Certificate (Knowledge) - Fibre Optics Installation conducted by James Contractor Pte. Ltd."
       , "(f) The Fibre Optic Installation and Maintenance course conducted by the Singtel Training Academy"
       , "(g) The Certificate of Competency for Fibre Optics Cabling Installer conducted by Republic Polytechnic"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`WW First Schedule item 1: the qualifications on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2024) THEN JUST (`WW First Schedule item 1 (Optical fibre cable), second column, as made by S 559/2024 (1 July 2024)`)
           OTHERWISE JUST (`WW First Schedule item 1 (Optical fibre cable), second column, as amended by S 852/2024 (11 November 2024)`)

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:240 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:241 | Regulation 3(3)(c)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:243 | FEES
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:244 | 1. Application fee for a telecommunication wiring . $30
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:245 | installer class licence
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:246 | 2. Application fee for a telecommunication wiring $100
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:247 | contractor class licence
@ref WW Second Schedule: fees (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:240-247)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`WW Second Schedule: the application fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 30   -- a telecommunication wiring installer class licence
           IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 100  -- a telecommunication wiring contractor class licence
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:249 | THIRD SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:250 | Regulation 4(2)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:252 | CONDITIONS OF TELECOMMUNICATION WIRING
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:253 | INSTALLER CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:254 | 1. A licensed installer must comply with the provisions of the Act, these
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:255 | Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:256 | 2. A licensed installer must not carry out any wiring work in relation to a type of
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:257 | wiring that the licensed installer is not authorised under regulation 4(1) to carry
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:258 | out.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:259 | 3. A licensed installer must notify the Authority of any change in the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:260 | information provided to the Authority under regulation 3(1) within 14 days
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:261 | after the change.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:262 | 4. A licensed installer must maintain a record of all wiring work that the licensed
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:263 | installer carries out on or after 1 July 2024 (unless the wiring work was carried out
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:266 | THIRD SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:267 | for a licensed contractor), for a period of at least 12 months after the date of
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:268 | completion of the wiring work, and the record must specify at least the following:
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:269 | (a) the type of wiring in relation to which the wiring work was carried out;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:270 | (b) the address of the premises where the wiring work was carried out.
@ref WW Third Schedule: conditions of installer class licence, items 1 to 4 (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:249-270)
GIVEN `the licensed installer complies with the Act, these Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed installer carries out no wiring work in relation to a type of wiring it is not authorised under regulation 4(1) to carry out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed installer notified the Authority of any change in the information under regulation 3(1) within 14 days after the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed installer maintains a record of all wiring work carried out on or after 1 July 2024 for at least 12 months after completion, with the type of wiring and the address of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW Third Schedule items 1 to 4: the licensed installer is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `the licensed installer complies with the Act, these Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work`
    AND `the licensed installer carries out no wiring work in relation to a type of wiring it is not authorised under regulation 4(1) to carry out`
    AND `the licensed installer notified the Authority of any change in the information under regulation 3(1) within 14 days after the change`
    AND `the licensed installer maintains a record of all wiring work carried out on or after 1 July 2024 for at least 12 months after completion, with the type of wiring and the address of the premises`

-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:272 | FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:273 | Regulation 5(2)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:275 | CONDITIONS OF TELECOMMUNICATION WIRING
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:276 | CONTRACTOR CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:277 | 1. A licensed contractor must comply with the provisions of the Act, these
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:278 | Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:279 | 2. A licensed contractor must be or must employ a licensed installer who is
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:280 | authorised under regulation 4(1) to carry out wiring work in relation to the type of
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:281 | wiring that the licensed contractor is authorised under regulation 5(1) to provide.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:282 | 3. A licensed contractor must, in carrying on the business of providing wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:283 | work, ensure that —
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:284 | (a) only a licensed installer (whose licence is not suspended) carries out
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:285 | the wiring work; and
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:286 | (b) the licensed installer only carries out wiring work in relation to the type
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:287 | of wiring that the licensed installer is authorised under regulation 4(1)
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:288 | to carry out.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:289 | 4. A licensed contractor must notify the Authority of any change in the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:290 | information provided to the Authority under regulation 3(2) within 14 days after
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:291 | the change.
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:292 | 5. A licensed contractor must maintain a record of all wiring work that the
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:293 | licensed contractor carries out or causes to be carried out on or after 1 July 2024,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:294 | for a period of at least 12 months after the date of completion of the wiring work,
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:295 | and the record must specify at least the following:
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:296 | (a) the particulars of the licensed installer who carried out the wiring
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:297 | work, including the licensed installer’s name and licence number;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:298 | (b) the type of wiring in relation to which the wiring work was carried out;
-- src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:299 | (c) the address of the premises where the wiring work was carried out.
@ref WW Fourth Schedule: conditions of contractor class licence, items 1 to 5 (S 559/2024) (src:TA1999-WW-S559-2024:272-299)
GIVEN `the licensed contractor complies with the Act, these Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed contractor is or employs a licensed installer authorised under regulation 4(1) for the type of wiring the contractor is authorised under regulation 5(1) to provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed contractor ensures that only a licensed installer whose licence is not suspended carries out the wiring work, and only for the type of wiring that installer is authorised to carry out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed contractor notified the Authority of any change in the information under regulation 3(2) within 14 days after the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensed contractor maintains a record of all wiring work carried out or caused to be carried out on or after 1 July 2024 for at least 12 months after completion, with the installer's particulars, the type of wiring and the address of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`WW Fourth Schedule items 1 to 5: the licensed contractor is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `the licensed contractor complies with the Act, these Regulations and the Code of Practice for Telecommunication Wiring Work`
    AND `the licensed contractor is or employs a licensed installer authorised under regulation 4(1) for the type of wiring the contractor is authorised under regulation 5(1) to provide`
    AND `the licensed contractor ensures that only a licensed installer whose licence is not suspended carries out the wiring work, and only for the type of wiring that installer is authorised to carry out`
    AND `the licensed contractor notified the Authority of any change in the information under regulation 3(2) within 14 days after the change`
    AND `the licensed contractor maintains a record of all wiring work carried out or caused to be carried out on or after 1 July 2024 for at least 12 months after completion, with the installer's particulars, the type of wiring and the address of the premises`
